; soak-prep: mount and format the two partitions on unit 4 (after any
; vscsitest run: it writes to every unit), copy the reference hashes, and
; record free memory. Then start, as three jobs at once:
;   Execute SHARED:vscsi/soakfs VS4A ffs 150
;   Execute SHARED:vscsi/soakfs VS4B sfs 150
;   Execute SHARED:vscsi/soakraw 100
FailAt 30
Copy SHARED:vscsi/vscsitest RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:vscsitest +rwed QUIET
Mount VS4A: FROM SHARED:vscsi/vs4.mountlist
Mount VS4B: FROM SHARED:vscsi/vs4.mountlist
Echo "" >RAM:cr
SYS:System/Format <RAM:cr DRIVE VS4A: NAME FFSTest QUICK NOICONS >NIL:
SYS:System/Format <RAM:cr DRIVE VS4B: NAME SFSTest QUICK NOICONS >NIL:
CD SYS:Libs
C:MD5Sum #? >SHARED:vscsi/soak/src.md5
CD RAM:
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Avail TOTAL >SHARED:vscsi/soak/mem-start.txt
Info VS4A:
Info VS4B:
